          "grammar_note": "A hangul block = consonant + vowel (+ optional final consonant). Example: ㅎ + ㅏ + ㄴ = 한. Korean has TWO number systems: Sino-Korean (일이삼...) for dates, money, phone numbers, minutes; Native Korean (하나둘셋...) for ages, hours, and counting objects with counters (개, 명, 권).",
